          "when": "Illinois exemptions are allowable and the asset is personal property used for personal rather than business purposes.",
          "procedure": "Always evaluate 735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(b): report the lesser of value and $4,000 for one debtor, or the lesser of value and $8,000 for two equal-interest joint debtors. Independently retain subsection (a) for necessary wearing apparel at whole asset value, subsection (c) for a motor vehicle at the lesser of whole asset value and $2,400, and subsection (e) for a professionally prescribed health aid at whole asset value.",
          "avoid_when": "Do not omit subsection (b) when a specific subsection applies or the asset exceeds $4,000, double subsection (c)'s $2,400 asset-level result merely because there are two debtors, omit subsection (a) because apparel exceeds another jurisdiction's clothing limit, treat personal-use tools as tools of trade without a business-use fact, or leave a half-interest as the final amount.",
